WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.281
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.581 --> 00:00:09.002
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.302 --> 00:00:15.507
Unit thirty-two: Superlatives (the biggest). Today you will say which thing is the most or the least.

4
00:00:15.807 --> 00:00:18.436
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:23.004
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:24.828
The biggest.

7
00:00:25.817 --> 00:00:28.165
The biggest means larger than all the others.

8
00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.262
It is the biggest city.

9
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:33.537
Your turn. Say: The biggest.

10
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.482
The biggest.

11
00:00:38.217 --> 00:00:39.276
The tallest.

12
00:00:40.283 --> 00:00:42.666
The tallest means higher than all the others.

13
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:44.878
He is the tallest boy.

14
00:00:45.483 --> 00:00:47.985
Your turn. Say: The tallest.

15
00:00:50.833 --> 00:00:51.962
The tallest.

16
00:00:52.717 --> 00:00:53.857
The fastest.

17
00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:57.349
The fastest means quicker than all the others.

18
00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:00.019
A cheetah is the fastest animal.

19
00:01:00.617 --> 00:01:03.397
Your turn. Say: The fastest.

20
00:01:06.233 --> 00:01:07.432
The fastest.

21
00:01:08.183 --> 00:01:09.556
The most beautiful.

22
00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:13.780
The most beautiful means nicer to look at than all the others.

23
00:01:14.383 --> 00:01:16.348
It is the most beautiful temple.

24
00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.776
Your turn. Say: The most beautiful.

25
00:01:22.633 --> 00:01:23.913
The most beautiful.

26
00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:25.593
The best.

27
00:01:26.583 --> 00:01:28.954
The best means better than all the others.

28
00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:31.050
She is the best student.

29
00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:34.685
Your turn. Say: The best.

30
00:01:37.533 --> 00:01:38.523
The best.

31
00:01:39.283 --> 00:01:40.203
The worst.

32
00:01:41.217 --> 00:01:43.437
The worst means worse than all the others.

33
00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:45.550
That was the worst day.

34
00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:48.663
Your turn. Say: The worst.

35
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:52.339
The worst.

36
00:01:53.083 --> 00:01:54.038
Of all.

37
00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:57.549
Of all means among everyone or everything.

38
00:01:58.150 --> 00:01:59.720
She is the kindest of all.

39
00:02:00.317 --> 00:02:02.563
Your turn. Say: Of all.

40
00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:06.413
Of all.

41
00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:08.314
Superlative.

42
00:02:09.317 --> 00:02:13.429
Superlative means the form that shows the highest or the lowest degree.

43
00:02:14.017 --> 00:02:16.086
The tallest is a superlative.

44
00:02:16.683 --> 00:02:19.440
Your turn. Say: Superlative.

45
00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:23.406
Superlative.

46
00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:27.770
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:28.617 --> 00:02:31.417
Visal, who is the tallest person in your family?

48
00:02:32.517 --> 00:02:42.219
My father is the tallest. We use the superlative to compare three or more things. Short adjectives take -est: tall, the tallest.

49
00:02:43.317 --> 00:02:45.142
What about long adjectives?

50
00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:57.345
Use the most before a long adjective: the most beautiful, the most expensive. Good becomes the best, and bad becomes the worst. These are irregular.

51
00:02:58.450 --> 00:02:59.614
How do we say where?

52
00:03:00.717 --> 00:03:13.472
We use in or of: the tallest in the class, the best of all. We always use the before a superlative. Spelling matters: big, the biggest; happy, the happiest.

53
00:03:14.633 --> 00:03:16.203
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:22.138
Grammar focus: Superlatives: the plus -est and the most plus adjective.

55
00:03:22.438 --> 00:03:23.671
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:24.383 --> 00:03:26.673
My father is the tallest in my family.

57
00:03:27.583 --> 00:03:29.943
This is the most beautiful temple in town.

58
00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:32.211
She is the best of all.

59
00:03:33.167 --> 00:03:41.882
Use the + -est for short adjectives and the most + adjective for long ones. Good is the best and bad is the worst. Use in or of for the group.

60
00:03:42.617 --> 00:03:46.070
Be careful! Don't say: It is the most big city.

61
00:03:48.033 --> 00:03:50.219
Say: It is the biggest city.

62
00:03:50.519 --> 00:03:52.983
Use -est with short adjectives.

63
00:03:53.767 --> 00:03:56.454
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:57.267 --> 00:03:58.744
The Best and the Biggest.

65
00:03:59.044 --> 00:04:01.705
The cheetah is the fastest animal in the world.

66
00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:05.048
Phnom Penh is the biggest city in Cambodia.

67
00:04:06.033 --> 00:04:08.497
Angkor Wat is the most famous temple.

68
00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:12.277
My sister is the best student in her class.

69
00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:15.104
That was the worst storm of the year.

70
00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:20.306
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:23.312
She is the blank girl in the class.

72
00:04:23.612 --> 00:04:26.627
A, tall. B, taller. C, tallest.

73
00:04:30.167 --> 00:04:31.946
The answer is C: tallest.

74
00:04:33.083 --> 00:04:35.013
This is the blank beautiful temple.

75
00:04:35.313 --> 00:04:38.154
A, most. B, more. C, much.

76
00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:43.374
The answer is A: most.

77
00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:45.982
He is blank best player.

78
00:04:46.282 --> 00:04:49.181
A, a. B, the. C, an.

79
00:04:52.733 --> 00:04:54.210
The answer is B: the.

80
00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:56.943
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:57.243 --> 00:05:03.625
A, It is the most big city.. B, It is the biggest city.. C, It is the bigest city..

82
00:05:07.167 --> 00:05:09.607
The answer is B: It is the biggest city..

83
00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:14.375
According to the reading, which city is the biggest in Cambodia?

84
00:05:14.675 --> 00:05:18.503
A, Phnom Penh. B, Siem Reap. C, Battambang.

85
00:05:22.067 --> 00:05:23.857
The answer is A: Phnom Penh.

86
00:05:25.067 --> 00:05:28.532
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:29.383 --> 00:05:31.882
Who is the tallest person in your family?

88
00:05:40.683 --> 00:05:42.160
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:56.830
My uncle is the tallest person in my family. He is taller than my father and taller than all my cousins. I use the tallest because I compare more than two people, and I always use the before a superlative.

90
00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:59.002
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:59.917 --> 00:06:05.715
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and superlatives: the plus -est and the most plus adjective.

92
00:06:06.015 --> 00:06:09.480
Today's value is pride in learning. Be proud of what you learned.

93
00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:12.827
See you in Unit thirty-three. Goodbye!

94
00:06:13.127 --> 00:06:16.674
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

